{"time": "2026-06-08T23:12:52", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "e_mixed_emergent_drift_g001_a02_d3fd5dae_004", "post_id": "7gqihu9", "subreddit": "worldnews", "content": "Every time I look at the news about Ukraine, it feels like I’m reading a press release instead of actual reporting. One week we’re told some new weapon system is going to completely turn the tide, and then a month later the front lines haven't budged and we're just on to the next hype cycle. It’s hard to get a straight answer on how things are actually going when every story is polished to death. Anyone else notice this or am I just cynical?"}
